message: "If you use Witness, please cite it as below."
title: "Witness: Do LLM auditors know when evidence cannot settle a claim about an agent run?"
type: software
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-11-16
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/wesdalton/witness"
url: "https://wesdalton.github.io/witness/"
authors:
  - family-names: Dalton
    given-names: Wesley
keywords:
  - LLM evaluation
  - AI auditing
  - agent evaluation
  - abstention
abstract: "A controlled benchmark of paired valid and invalid agent-evaluation runs whose evidence is byte-identical under restricted access, used to test whether LLM auditors recognize insufficient evidence and use the evidence that can settle a claim. In a pre-registered study on held-out tasks, two auditors accepted test runs whose replay showed exit status 0 with no test summary, and committed to verdicts on reports that could not decide the claim."
